      "id": "bug-089",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-05T00:00:00.000Z",
      "error_message": "Admin panel stayed locked (RateUpdateGate) even after the user entered today's silver/gold rate and clicked Update Rate",
      "file": "src/routes/admin.routes.ts, src/middlewares/auth.middleware.ts",
      "root_cause": "admin.routes.ts applies a blanket `router.use(protect, admin)` to every route in the file, and `admin` middleware only checks `req.user.isAdmin`. The rate-update endpoints (`POST /admin/silver-rates`, `POST /admin/gold-rates`) and `GET /admin/rate-status` lived under that blanket gate, so a `staff` user's update request 403'd silently (frontend shows a generic toast) and the rate was never actually persisted — the lock could never clear for staff, no matter how many times they 'updated' it. The frontend's own RateUpdateGate explicitly says the lock applies to 'all admin and staff' and renders the update form to both, so this was a genuine spec/implementation mismatch, not just the previously-documented 'staff carve-out not shipped yet' limitation.",
      "fix": "Added `adminOrStaff` middleware (isAdmin OR role==='staff') in auth.middleware.ts. Registered GET/POST /silver-rates, GET/POST /gold-rates, and GET /rate-status with `protect, adminOrStaff` explicitly, positioned before the blanket `router.use(protect, admin)` in the same router so they match first and never hit the stricter blanket gate. All other /admin/* routes remain isAdmin-only. Updated 6 existing test files' auth.middleware mocks to stub adminOrStaff (route registration otherwise throws at import time), and added src/tests/rate-staff-access.api.test.ts using the real middleware to regression-test staff access + confirm plain customers still get 403.",
      "tags": [
        "auth",
        "rbac",
        "staff",
        "admin-panel",
        "rate-lock",
        "silver-rate",
        "gold-rate",
        "403"
      ],
      "related_bugs": [],
      "occurrences": 1,
      "last_seen": "2026-07-05T00:00:00.000Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "bug-090",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-05T00:00:00.000Z",
      "error_message": "Staff login could open the admin panel UI but got 403 Forbidden on almost every request: /admin/stats, /admin/orders, /admin/users, /admin/savings, /admin/coupons, /admin/returns, /admin/inventory/*, /admin/delivery-config",
      "file": "src/routes/admin.routes.ts",
      "root_cause": "router.use(protect, admin) blanket-applied isAdmin-only auth to the entire admin.routes.ts router, but the frontend Admin.tsx clearly built most tabs for staff too (queries enabled for role==='admin'||'staff', no per-action role gating on buttons, one tab's own comment said 'staff can manage delivery fees'). Browser-verified via Playwright: logging in as the seeded staff account and opening /admin produced 30 console errors, nearly all 403s.",
      "fix": "User decision: staff should mirror admin everywhere except inventory. Changed the blanket to router.use(protect, adminOrStaff). Re-restricted store-config, pricing-config, gift-vouchers (no staff-facing UI / financially sensitive) and all inventory/* routes (explicit product decision) back to admin-only via an explicit `admin` middleware added on each of those routes (stacks on top of the looser blanket, since Express runs per-route middleware after router.use() middleware regardless of the blanket's own permissiveness). Frontend: inventory queries changed to enabled: role==='admin' only, and the Inventory tab hidden from staff in Admin.tsx. Regression tests added/updated in rate-staff-access.api.test.ts.",
